Modifications for the HNN CN ET build:
  Copyright (c) 2026 ET

These modifications are also licensed under the MIT License. They include:
  * Branding: user-facing application name changed to "HNN CN ET"
    (package name, MNN library identifiers and technical attribution unchanged).
  * 32-bit (armeabi-v7a) and 64-bit (arm64-v8a) native ABI packaging. The core
    libraries (libMNN / libmnnllmapp / libmnn_tts) ship for both ABIs.
  * Speech recognition parity on 32-bit: libsherpa-mnn-jni.so for armeabi-v7a is
    compiled from the sherpa-mnn source bundled in alibaba/MNN 3.6.0
    (apps/frameworks/sherpa-mnn, derived from k2-fsa sherpa-onnx). Its 94 JNI
    exports match the arm64-v8a prebuilt exactly; the runtime load is guarded so
    a missing native lib disables ASR gracefully instead of crashing.
  * In-app self-update against this repository's GitHub Releases (resumable,
    with retry, progress/speed dialog and system installer integration).
  * Built-in on-device application log viewer (level filter, keyword filter,
    copy all, system share, uncaught-exception capture).
  * Settings entries: "Contact Author" (mailto:2416444244@qq.com) and
    "Join QQ Group".
  * Model download robustness: automatic redirect following, explicit read/write
    timeouts, correct HTTP 206 resume vs 200 restart handling, larger transfer
    buffer (existing retry, SHA/etag verification and speed reporting retained).

